<title>CHINA: China's '97 oil-bearing crop seen at 23-23.5 mln T.</title>
<headline>China's '97 oil-bearing crop seen at 23-23.5 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's harvest of oil-bearing crops is expected to reach 23-23.5 million tonnes in 1997, the Futures Herald newspaper said on Thursday quoting a forecast by the Ministry of Internal Trade.</p>
<p>China produced 22 million tonnes of edible oil crops last year, down 1.7 percent from the previous year, official figures show. Output included 10.1 million tonnes of peanuts and 9.1 million tonnes of rapeseed.</p>
<p>The projected increase was mainly due to an expansion of 180,009 hectares of land planted with oil crops in 1997, the paper said, without giving further details.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
</text>
